yupiter licenses
===================

This directory documents every license that applies to the yupiter
repository.  The library is multi licensed: every recipient may
choose between three licenses, per use, at no cost.


The three licenses
------------------

GPL-2.0-or-later (GPLv2+)
-------------------------

Full text: GPL-2.0.txt

The GNU General Public License, version 2 or any later version.  A
program that contains or is derived from yupiter and is distributed
must be distributed in total under a GPL-compatible license: in
practice, under the GPL family itself, with the source code offered to
the recipients.

The "or any later version" option is granted by the copyright holder
of this project, and is stated in the header of every source file.

LGPL-2.1-or-later (LGPLv2+)
---------------------------

Full text: LGPL-2.1.txt

The GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or any later
version.  The LGPL applies to yupiter itself.  A program that merely
uses the library (for example, links against libyupiter.so) stays under
the license chosen by its own author, including a proprietary license.

The obligations of the LGPL on the user of the library are, in short:

* Any work that uses the library must let the user relink it against
  a modified version of the library.  For dynamic linking against
  libyupiter.so this is automatic.  For static linking against
  libyupiter.a, the LGPL requires that the user can perform the relink,
  for example by shipping the object files or by using a shared
  library.

* Any modified version of the library itself must be released in
  total under the LGPL.

* The unmodified library must remain available in its unmodified form,
  and the notices of the library must be preserved.

The precise and legally binding conditions are in LGPL-2.1.txt,
section 4 ("Modified Versions"), section 5 ("Combining a Modified
Work with the Library") and section 6 ("Combining Applications with
the Library").  Read them before redistributing.

Apache-2.0
----------

Full text: Apache-2.0.txt

The Apache License, Version 2.0.  A permissive license with an
explicit patent grant from the contributors.  A work that contains or
is derived from yupiter may be distributed under any license,
including a proprietary license, with no obligation to release the
source code of your own work.

This option is the right choice when your project must link against
yupiter statically, for example because shared objects or DLLs are
not an option in your environment: the Apache License imposes no
conditions on linking at all, static or dynamic.  The conditions of
redistribution are limited to keeping the notices, stating changes to
modified files, and including a copy of the license.

The patent grant of section 3 includes a termination clause: a
licensee who patent sues anyone over the licensed code loses their
rights under the license.

Note on compatibility: the Apache License 2.0 is one-way incompatible
with the GNU GPL version 2, so a combined work may not be distributed
under GPLv2.  Because the GPL option of yupiter is "version 2 or any
later version", you may distribute such a combination under GPLv3
instead, which accepts Apache-2.0 code.


How the choice works
--------------------

* The choice belongs to whoever redistributes the library or a work
  containing it.  Choosing one license does not remove the other
  options: the next recipient may still pick any of the three.

* A contribution to this project is accepted under the same multi
  licensing: the contributor grants the right to distribute the
  contribution under all three licenses.  By contributing you confirm
  that the contribution is your own work and that you grant this
  permission.

* The header of every source file in this repository carries the
  multi-license notice.  A file copied out of the tree keeps its
  licensing information; do not remove the header.


